# ============================================================
# Development-mode build config (vite build --mode development)
# Used by `pnpm build:dev` → deploy:dev → dev.mercurypitch.com
# ============================================================

# Cloud DB API (mercury-pitch-db-dev worker), on its dedicated custom
# subdomain so the Google OAuth consent screen shows a mercurypitch.com host
# instead of workers.dev. A dedicated host — not a /api/* route on the shared
# domain — avoids shadowing the main worker's /api/uvr/* and /api/share/*
# (see workers/db-worker/wrangler.jsonc routes). Activates the HybridAdapter
# on dev.mercurypitch.com:
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api-dev.mercurypitch.com

# Cloudflare Turnstile PUBLIC site key. Not a secret — it is rendered into the
# page by the widget. Its private half lives on the db-worker as the
# TURNSTILE_SECRET binding (wrangler secret, never in this repo).
#
# This value is what ARMS the CAPTCHA on the client. The worker gate fails
# CLOSED once TURNSTILE_SECRET is set, so if the secret is set and this is
# missing, the widget never renders, no token is ever sent, and every
# register / login / forgot-password returns 400. Set both, or neither.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAADwxFpbIS2KUOInz

# Glassworks, the museum campaign, is listed here: a Home card, a Home tour
# step, and the sitemap / llms.txt / prelude links. The production web build
# serves /glass-game but lists none of it — see .env.production and
# tools/glassworks-listing.ts. `pnpm dev` reads this file too.
VITE_GLASSWORKS_LISTED=1

# Find Your Pitch's draft lessons (src/features/lessons/kit/drafts.ts: today
# Lessons 3 and 5, waiting on the vocal coach) are linked by default on a
# page that no worker served with the admin console's state: `pnpm dev`
# reads this file too. Every build carries every lesson page; on
# dev.mercurypitch.com and PR previews the site worker serves them with the
# console's state and its own default, which shows drafts too (LESSON_DRAFTS
# in wrangler.jsonc, src/lesson-gate.ts). See .env.production and
# tools/draft-lessons.ts.
VITE_DRAFT_LESSONS=1

# Retention periods for the ids this browser holds: see .env.production.
VITE_RETENTION_CLICK_ID_DAYS=90
VITE_RETENTION_FUNNEL_ID_MONTHS=13

# Experimental features (Studio first) are on here: the nav tab, its tour and
# the sitemap / llms.txt / prelude links. The production web build and the
# native app keep them off, and the owner can switch one either way per
# environment from his console. See .env.production and
# tools/experimental-features.ts. `pnpm dev` reads this file too.
VITE_EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES=1
